# AGENTS.md additions — absorbed 2026-06-20 from
# KooshaPari/pheno-cargo-template/template/AGENTS.md.additions.
#
# This fragment is appended to a generated crate's AGENTS.md by the
# `pheno-scaffold-kit` post-generate hook. It codifies the agent
# conventions that apply to every scaffolded crate.

## HexaKit `hexagon/rust` crate conventions (auto-appended by scaffold-kit)

### File layout

- `src/lib.rs` — public surface (the only file scaffolded).
- `src/<module>/` — private modules; each `<= 350` lines (target) and
  `<= 500` lines (hard limit). Decompose proactively.
- `tests/` — `unit/`, `integration/`, `e2e/` (no `_v2`, `_final`, `_new`).
- `docs/sessions/` — session-based work artifacts; never at repo root.

### Quality gates (cargo workspace)

- `cargo fmt --all -- --check` — idempotent format check.
- `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings`.
- `cargo test --workspace`.
- `cargo deny check` — advisories + bans + licenses + sources.
- 80% lib coverage gate (ADR-023 Rule 3.1).

### Conventional Commits

- `feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `docs:`, `refactor:`, `test:`, `perf:`,
  `build:`, `ci:`, `style:`, `revert:`.
- Every commit references a task ID (`T-…`) when one is assigned.

### Absorb anchor

- Keep `crate_name()`, `template_source()`, and `absorbed_from()`
  exported from `src/lib.rs` unless the absorb anchor is intentionally
  rewritten during a fork.